build*/
*.o
*.d
.DS_Store
dist/
*.dmg
third_party/

# Sparkle's private update signing key. It normally lives only in the login
# keychain, so there is nothing here to ignore — these patterns exist for the
# moment someone exports it with `generate_keys -x` to make a backup and
# leaves the file in the working tree. Whoever holds this key can hand every
# installed copy arbitrary code as a signed update.
*.private-key
sparkle_private*
dsa_priv.pem
